H2: Known Faults - Mazda 2
P: The sources cover the second generation (2007-2015) and the third generation (2015-2025), and some write about all generations at once. Each fault below says which car it concerns where the source does.
H3: Air Conditioning
P: MONITOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: FixMyCar says the air conditioning system is problematic in both the second and third generations of the Mazda 2. Auto Express, writing about the 2015-2025 car, says one of the more common gripes is faulty air-con. The RAC, on the 2015-2019 car, says a few issues have been raised about the air conditioning system: it should kick out ice cold air, but may not. On a test drive, run it on its coldest setting and feel the air from the vents.
H3: Diesel Particulate Filter
P: MONITOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: FixMyCar says diesel models can suffer from a blocked diesel particulate filter (DPF) if used for many short journeys. Auto Express goes further for the 2015-2025 car and says not to buy a diesel Mazda 2 unless you regularly undertake long journeys, because short trips are known to clog up the filter. Ask the seller what sort of journeys the car has done.
H3: Sensors and Carbon Build-Up
P: MONITOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: FixMyCar says second- and third-generation cars also see the odd ABS sensor failure and carbon build-up, alongside the air conditioning faults. It adds that sensor failures are not uncommon in older Mazda 2 models. Look for warning lights on the dash when you switch the ignition on, and make sure they go out.
H3: Clutch
P: MINOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: For the 2015-2019 car, the RAC advises checking that there isn't any slippage or notchy feel from the clutch. Carbuyer's guide to the 2007-2015 car says many owners report that the clutch pedal clicks when it is depressed, although it calls this a niggling idiosyncrasy rather than a fault per se.
H3: Sat-Nav and Climate Control Electrics
P: MINOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says a few owners of the 2015-2019 car reported small niggles relating to non-engine electrics, centring on the sat-nav and the climate control. Try the screen, the sat-nav and the heating controls before you agree a price.
H3: Misting Windows
P: MINOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyer says the windows of the 2007-2015 Mazda2 are known to mist up easily, although running the air-conditioning year-round cures this. If you buy one, check that the air conditioning works so that the cure is available to you.
H3: Safety Recalls
P: CHECK ú Any miles ú Ask a Mazda dealer
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Mazda2 recalls, including these.
LI: The impeller in the low-pressure fuel pump may become deformed, causing fuel pump failure.
LI: Passenger airbag inflators may not operate as intended.
LI: The engine protection logic does not work properly on the vehicles concerned.
LI: The tolerances of the teeth on the handbrake sector gear are outside Mazda Corporation's design specifications.
LI: The surface finishing of the brake hose retaining clip may be insufficient, causing a possibility of corrosion and failure of the clip.
LI: The lower nut and bolt securing the front shock absorber to the steering knuckle on either side may not have been tightened to specification.
LI: Silicone may have adhered to the welding surface of the roll-over valve (ROV) fitted to the fuel tank.
P: DVSA lists these under the names Mazda2, MAZDA 2 and 2, so the data doesn't say which generation each one covers. Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a particular car has work outstanding.
H2: Buying a used Mazda 2
P: FixMyCar says there aren't any universally agreed years to avoid, but that reliability data and workshop experience suggest being selective about certain engine and age combinations. It says the 2019-present car has very few common issues. What Car? gives the 2015-2025 Mazda 2 a reliability rating of 96.4%, and Carbuyer says the 2007-2015 car has an excellent reputation for reliability. In Carbuyer's 2022 Driver Power customer satisfaction survey, Mazda as a brand was ranked seventh overall out of 29 makers, and Carbuyer says Mazda has forged a strong reputation for building durable cars.
P: Whichever generation you choose, ask for the service history, run through the checks above on a test drive, and check recall work has been done. The RAC also suggests checking the alloys for parking scuffs. For parts and garage prices, see our Mazda 2 parts guide .
H2: Breakdown cover
P: If a fault stops the car on the road, breakdown cover sends help to you. Compare two UK providers and check what each policy includes.
P: We earn a commission if you buy cover through these links, at no cost to you ( how we're paid ).
H2: Mazda 2 MOT results in 2025
P: There were 126,328 MOT tests of the Mazda 2 in 2025. 30.5% failed first time, against 27.7% for all cars. Older cars fail more often, so the fairer comparison is by age:
H3: What they failed on
LI: Suspension : 13.0% of tests (all cars 9.0%). Shock absorber prices
LI: Lamps, reflectors and electrical equipment : 11.4% of tests (all cars 10.6%). Headlight bulb prices by type
LI: Tyres : 6.1% of tests (all cars 6.2%)
LI: Visibility : 5.8% of tests (all cars 4.3%). Wiper blade prices
LI: Brakes : 4.6% of tests (all cars 6.2%). Brake pad prices , brake disc prices
P: Initial MOT tests in Great Britain, 2025, from DVSA's anonymised MOT data; fail rate as DVSA calculates it (fails plus faults fixed during the test). Results cover every car recorded under the model name, so the older age bands can include earlier generations of it. Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0. MOT pass rates for every model and how they're worked out .
