H2: Known Faults - Mazda 3
H3: Infotainment and Bluetooth
P: MONITOR ú 2009 on ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyer says the Bluetooth system on the 2009-2014 car has been reported to have trouble pairing with some phones, and in certain cases a dealer can update the car's software to resolve the issue. Auto Express says some owners of the 2008-2013 car have reported problems with getting the Bluetooth system to talk to their phone. For the 2014-2019 car, it has seen the odd report of minor glitches with the infotainment system and sat-nav. What Car? says a few petrol owners of the 2019 on car mentioned occasional electrical faults, such as malfunctioning infotainment screens and sensor warnings, but these were typically minor and easily resolved.
H3: Diesel Particulate Filter
P: MONITOR ú 2009 on ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says the 2.0-litre diesel engine's diesel particulate filter can fail to regenerate itself on the 2009-2011 car. On the 2013-2018 diesels, it says the filter can cause problems, especially if you accidentally shut it off partway through its regeneration cycle. Auto Express says diesel particulate filters can clog up on 2014-2019 cars used only for short trips. For the 2019 on car, What Car? says some diesel models have been less reliable, with issues including warning lights for the diesel particulate filter (DPF) and problems with the emissions system.
H3: Diesel Injectors
P: MONITOR ú 2009-2013 ú Get a quote
P: In its review of the 2009-2013 car, What Car? says 1.6-litre diesel models have been known to suffer with injector faults.
H3: Early 2.0-litre Petrol Engine
P: MONITOR ú 2009-2013 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says early examples of the 2.0-litre MZR/L engine could suffer from high oil consumption and bore wear. Its review covers the 2009-2013 car.
H3: MPS Suspension Alignment
P: CHECK ú 2011-2013 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says that on the 2011-2013 car the MPS model is very susceptible to misaligned suspension, so check for uneven tyre wear.
H3: Boot-Release Button Cover
P: MINOR ú 2009-2014 ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyer says the 2009-2014 car has a rubber cover over the boot-release button, which dries out and cracks.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Mazda3 recalls, including these.
LI: On affected vehicles the images from the rear view / 360 cameras may not display.
LI: The plastic logo on the steering wheel centre may shatter and project fragments into the vehicle interior during an air bag deployment.
LI: The engine may stall or fail to restart in some driving situations.
LI: Vehicles may unexpectedly stop due to inadvertent activation of the automated Smart Brake Support (SBS) system.
LI: Software controlling the engine air / fuel ratio contains an error.
P: Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has a recall that is still open.
