H2: Known Faults - Mazda 6
P: The faults below come from reviews of the 2002-2007 car, the 2008-2012 car and the 2012-2022 car.
H3: Electrical Faults and Infotainment
P: MONITOR ú 2008-2022 ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyer says it has heard of electrical issues with the 2008-2012 generation of Mazda 6. For the 2012-2022 Tourer, its Driver Power survey found electrical issues the most common faults. What Car? says most of the reliability concerns on the 2013-2022 saloon were for minor electronic components and infotainment system glitches, which were occasionally troublesome but not severe.
H3: Diesel Particulate Filter
P: CHECK ú 2008-2022 ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyer says the 2.0-litre diesel in the 2008-2012 car has particular trouble with its diesel particulate filter clogging. For the 2012-2022 car it says DPF problems can appear if the filter is allowed to build up too much soot. In the RAC's ownership survey of the 2013-2018 car, one diesel buyer had DPF problems and also needed a new steering lock module. Autocar says to check the diesel particulate filter valve, especially on the 2.0-litre diesel if it has a lower than average mileage.
H3: 2.2 Diesel Timing Chain
P: HIGH ú 2008-2012 ú Get a quote
P: On the 2.2-litre diesel in the 2008-2012 car, Carbuyer says it has heard reports of the chain losing tension, which can result in major repair work under the bonnet.
H3: 2.0 Diesel Fuel in the Oil
P: CHECK ú 2007-2012 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the older 2.0-litre diesel engine can suffer with lubrication problems, where fuel finds its way into the oil system.
H3: Brake Discs
P: MONITOR ú 2013-2022 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the 2013-2022 saloon can be quite hard on its brake discs, which can lead to vibration under braking. It also says bodywork and brake system issues were the most commonly cited problems for the 31% of owners whose cars went wrong.
H3: Clutch
P: MONITOR ú 2002-2007 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says clutches on the 2002-2007 Mazda 6 have been a weak spot. A vibrating clutch has been a problem on diesels, but it says a visit to a dealer, who will fit a modified part, usually free of charge, cures it.
H3: Air-Con Evaporator
P: MINOR ú 2012 on ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says a manufacturing fault with the air-con evaporator could lead to white powder being emitted from the air vents, and that a new evaporator fixes things. Autocar also says to check for leaking air-con.
H3: 2.2 Diesel Idle
P: MINOR ú 2012 on ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says the 2.2-litre diesel engine can suffer from an erratic idle, but a software update should fix things with no damage likely to be caused.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Mazda 6 recalls, including these.
LI: Fuel may leak from fuel pump rings.
LI: The software controlling the hydraulic valve clearance adjuster may operate incorrectly.
LI: On the subject vehicles the Takata Driver and Passenger airbag inflators may not operate as intended. Injury may result due to incorrect deployment of the Airbag.
P: Check the car with our recall check .
