H2: Known Faults - Mazda CX-3
H3: Engine Cutting Out on Cars Built to April 2017
P: HIGH ú Built to April 2017 ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express, in its used review of the Mk1 CX-3 from 2015 to 2020, says CX-3s made up to April 2017 could suffer an electrical short circuit leading to the engine cutting out.
H3: Air-Conditioning and Climate Control
P: CHECK ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says many owners have experienced problems with the air-conditioning, and that dealers have been replacing systems under warranty.
H3: Diesel Particulate Filter on Low-Mileage Diesels
P: CHECK ú Low-mileage diesels ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express warns buyers to be wary when buying a low-mileage CX-3 diesel, because problems can occur if the DPF regeneration is interrupted.
H3: Electrics, Sat-Nav and Warning Lights
P: MONITOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: What Car?, reviewing the 2015-2019 CX-3, says owners reported small niggles only, mostly relating to non-engine electrics and centring on the sat-nav and the climate control.
P: One Parkers owner of a 1.5d SE-L Nav wrote that they got the car back before Christmas 2017 with warning lights on the dash and more time off the road.
H3: Rust Report From One Owner
P: MINOR ú One owner's report ú Get a quote
P: One Parkers owner of a 2.0 Sport Nav, who had the car from new, wrote that it was rusting already.
H3: Windscreen Washer Warning
P: MINOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says that if the windscreen washers do not work, the water reservoir is probably empty, and that there is no warning on the dashboard to tell you.
H3: Reliability Surveys and Owner Views
P: MINOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says that on the whole the Mazda CX-3 enjoys a good reliability record, with few specific problems. It adds that all problems were fixed within a week and under warranty.
P: What Car? says the CX-3 was absent from its latest reliability survey, but in the last one it appeared in, it finished 10th in the small SUV class.
P: Auto Express says the CX-3 ranked a disappointing 48th in the Driver Power 2018 new car satisfaction survey, with poor ratings for practicality, comfort and running costs dragging the score down.
P: Auto Express says build quality is excellent, especially on the inside, while Mazda's reputation for reliability should provide some peace of mind.
P: In a Parkers owner review, a 2.0 SE-L Nav Auto owner called it a very reliable car that drives and handles well. In another, the owner of a 2.0 Sport Nav was impressed with the quality of the interior and the pulling power of the 2.0 litre engine. The owner of a SkyActiv-D Sport Nav+ from 08/2018 on wrote that it handles very well and the gearchange is a joy.
P: To see whether a particular CX-3 has an outstanding DVSA safety recall, use our recall check ; the Mazda CX-3 parts guide sets out its engines, gearboxes and the 2018 update.
H2: Breakdown cover
P: If a fault stops the car on the road, breakdown cover sends help to you. Compare two UK providers and check what each policy includes.
P: We earn a commission if you buy cover through these links, at no cost to you ( how we're paid ).
H2: Mazda CX-3 MOT results in 2025
P: There were 25,302 MOT tests of the Mazda CX-3 in 2025. 16.5% failed first time, against 27.7% for all cars. Older cars fail more often, so the fairer comparison is by age:
H3: What they failed on
LI: Tyres : 4.4% of tests (all cars 6.2%)
LI: Suspension : 3.8% of tests (all cars 9.0%). Shock absorber prices
