H2: Frequently asked questions
P: What Car? says that on the whole the Mazda CX-3 enjoys a good reliability record, with few specific problems. Auto Express says it ranked a disappointing 48th in the Driver Power 2018 new car satisfaction survey, with poor ratings for practicality, comfort and running costs.
P: Auto Express says CX-3s made up to April 2017 could suffer an electrical short circuit leading to the engine cutting out, and that many owners have experienced problems with the air-conditioning. What Car? says owners reported small niggles only, mostly relating to non-engine electrics and centring on the sat-nav and the climate control.
P: Auto Express says to be wary when buying a low-mileage CX-3 diesel, because problems can occur if the DPF regeneration is interrupted.
P: Auto Express says that if the windscreen washers do not work, the water reservoir is probably empty, and there is no warning on the dashboard to tell you.
P: On Parkers, one owner of a 2.0 SE-L Nav Auto called it a very reliable car that drives and handles well. Another, who owns a 2.0 Sport Nav, wrote that they were impressed with the quality of the interior and the pulling power of the 2.0 litre engine.
