H2: Known Faults - Mazda CX-30
H3: 12-Volt Battery and Electrics, What Car? Survey
P: MONITOR ú 2020-present cars ú Get a quote
P: In its Reliability Survey of cars up to five years old, What Car? gives the Mazda CX-30 (2020-present) a reliability rating of 93.4%. Under most common faults it lists the 12-volt battery at 13%, followed by air-con, engine electrics, non-engine electrics and the sat-nav and infotainment system.
H3: Infotainment Freezing and Connection
P: MONITOR ú 2020-present cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says that in its used reliability review of the CX-30 a few issues emerged, particularly with the infotainment system, where some owners experienced freezing screens and intermittent connection problems.
H3: Warning Lights Appearing Unexpectedly
P: CHECK ú 2020-present cars ú Get a quote
P: A handful of What Car? readers mentioned warning lights appearing unexpectedly. What Car? adds that in most cases these issues were resolved quickly by dealers.
H3: Electrical Faults and Battery Drain, One Owner's Report
P: CHECK ú One owner's report ú Get a quote
P: A Parkers owner of a Skyactiv-X GT Sport, bought new in September 2020, wrote that the car has major electrical issues, that something is draining the battery and that the battery is also not keeping charge, which has led to several no starts. They wrote that this has been happening since they bought the car.
H3: Mirrors, Alarm and Battery Warning, One Owner's Report
P: CHECK ú One owner's report ú Get a quote
P: One Parkers owner of an e-Skyactiv-X MHEV Sport Lux wrote that the folding mirrors sometimes work, that a low battery warning comes on often, and that the alarm came on the other day when they were only a short way from the car after locking it.
H3: Emergency Braking and Boot Lid, One Owner's Report
P: CHECK ú One owner's report ú Get a quote
P: A Parkers owner of an e-Skyactiv-X MHEV Sport Lux wrote that the electrics are dodgy, that emergency braking came on a few times for no reason and that they have switched it off as too risky. They also wrote that the boot lid went up an hour before they went outside to the car.
H3: Warning Bongs, One Owner's Report
P: CHECK ú One owner's report ú Get a quote
P: A Parkers owner of an e-Skyactiv-X MHEV GT Sport automatic wrote that the various warning bongs became wearing, particularly as you were often left guessing what the warning was for.
H3: Reliability Survey Placing and Verdict
P: MINOR ú 2020-present cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says its data shows the Mazda CX-30 is a generally reliable car. In its 2024 What Car? Reliability Survey it ranked 16th out of 24 cars in the small SUV category, with a reliability score of 93.4%. Its verdict is that the CX-30 appears to be a reliable choice, with only minor faults reported.
P: Enter a registration in our recall check before you commit to a car, and use the Mazda CX-30 parts page for engines, power and gearbox details.
H2: Breakdown cover
P: If a fault stops the car on the road, breakdown cover sends help to you. Compare two UK providers and check what each policy includes.
P: We earn a commission if you buy cover through these links, at no cost to you ( how we're paid ).
H2: Mazda CX-30 MOT results in 2025
P: There were 20,897 MOT tests of the Mazda CX-30 in 2025. 8.7% failed first time, against 27.7% for all cars. Older cars fail more often, so the fairer comparison is by age:
H3: What they failed on
LI: Tyres : 3.0% of tests (all cars 6.2%)
LI: Visibility : 2.4% of tests (all cars 4.3%). Wiper blade prices
LI: Brakes : 1.8% of tests (all cars 6.2%). Brake pad prices , brake disc prices
LI: Lamps, reflectors and electrical equipment : 1.2% of tests (all cars 10.6%). Headlight bulb prices by type
LI: Suspension : 0.7% of tests (all cars 9.0%). Shock absorber prices
