H2: Frequently asked questions
P: What Car? says the CX-30 is a generally reliable car. In its 2024 Reliability Survey it ranked 16th out of 24 cars in the small SUV category, with a reliability score of 93.4%.
P: For the CX-30 (2020-present), What Car? lists the 12-volt battery as the most reported fault area at 13%. Air-con, engine electrics, non-engine electrics and the sat-nav and infotainment system follow it in the list.
P: In its used reliability review, What Car? says some owners experienced freezing screens and intermittent connection problems with the infotainment system. A handful of readers also mentioned warning lights appearing unexpectedly.
P: Parkers owners each wrote about their own car. One reported electrical issues and a battery drain, one wrote about folding mirrors, a low battery warning and an alarm, and one described emergency braking coming on for no reason.
