H2: Known Faults - Mazda CX-5
P: The faults below are split by the years each source gives: the 2012-2017 car and the 2017 on car.
H3: DPF Blockage
P: MONITOR ú 2012-2017 and 2017 on diesels ú œ202.49 average DPF clean (FixMyCar)
P: On the 2012-2017 car, Parkers says a blocked DPF will restrict exhaust flow and send the car into limp-home mode, and the owner will be shopping for a new particulate filter. It names cars which have been driven for short trips (less than 10 minutes between start and stop), at low speeds, or left idling for long periods. On the 2017 on car, What Car? says some diesel owners have faced challenges with the diesel particulate filter and exhaust systems, leading to visits to dealerships. FixMyCar says a garage will typically attempt to clean the DPF first, which costs œ202.49 on average for a CX-5.
H3: Fuel in the Engine Oil
P: MONITOR ú 2012-2017 diesels ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says some 2012-2017 diesels can suffer from fuel entering the sump if the engine is switched off when the DPF is regenerating, and that a rising engine oil level is the sign of it. Parkers says this causes unburned diesel to reach the engine oil, diluting it. Its advice when viewing one is to look at the level and condition of the oil and to sniff for diesel fumes.
H3: Intake Shutter Valve Soot
P: MONITOR ú Made 26 January 2012 to 30 June 2018 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says a soot build-up in the intake shutter valve in the engine could cause problems on models made from 26 January 2012 to 30 June 2018. DVSA's recall data includes a recall saying that soot may accumulate around the intake shutter valve on the inlet side of the engine.
H3: Bodywork and Electrical Faults
P: MINOR ú 2017 on ú œ132.82 average auto electrician repair (FixMyCar)
P: In What Car?'s survey of the 2017 on car, bodywork and electrical issues were the most common complaints. FixMyCar gives œ132.82 as the average price of a repair by an auto electrician on its site.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several CX-5 recalls, including these.
LI: Catalytic Reduction (SCR) system wiring may become damaged by contamination.
LI: One or both LED daytime Running Lamps may flicker flash or fail completely.
LI: Soot may accumulate around the intake shutter valve on the inlet side of the engine.
LI: The tightening force of the injector mounting nuts may be insufficient.
LI: The Software controlling the fuel injectors does not control the electric current correctly.
P: Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has a recall that is still open.
