H2: Frequently asked questions
P: The RAC says a well looked after late-shape Mk2 is a very safe used purchase, being both reliable and easy to sell on. Carbuyer says MX-5s are known for their brilliant reliability, so most gremlins are minor and rarely crop up. What Car? says most Mk4 owners reported few issues, and the RAC reports that a What Car? survey confirmed the roadster to be the most reliable car in Britain.
P: Octane names rust as the single biggest issue facing any Mk1, and Classic & Sports Car calls corrosion the Mk2&#39;s biggest enemy. Parkers says rust is a serious foe of older MX-5s. Autocar says Mk3 brake calipers are prone to seizing, and the RAC says it has heard of Mk4 gearbox issues with gear selection from 1st to 2nd and from 2nd to 3rd.
P: Yes. DVSA&#39;s recall data lists several MX-5 recalls, covering things such as fuel pipe brackets, the low-pressure fuel pump impeller, an under shield bracket and a driver&#39;s footwell floor mat. Enter the registration in our [recall check](/car-recall-check) to see whether a particular car has work outstanding.
P: Octane says to check that the Mk1 hood drain tubes ahead of the rear wheels are clear. Autocar says to brake hard on a Mk3 to check for pulling, and What Car? says an automatic car wash cycle will show whether a Mk4 roof leaks. The RAC says the Roadster Coupe roof should work quickly with no need for manual alignment.
